#===============================================================================
#  ARDHANARISHVARA OS — ENGINEERING SUPPORT DOCUMENT
#  SovereignOS Security Engine
#  File: security_engine.support
#===============================================================================
#  PURPOSE:
#    Engineering reference for the SovereignOS security engine responsible for:
#      • authentication tokens
#      • cryptographic hashing & HMAC
#      • permission enforcement
#      • audit logging
#      • threat classification
#
#===============================================================================
#  MODULE SUMMARY:
#
#    - [Auth Tokens](ca://s?q=Explain_Security_Auth_Tokens)
#    - [Cryptographic Hashing](ca://s?q=Explain_Cryptographic_Hashing)
#    - [HMAC Signatures](ca://s?q=Explain_HMAC_Signatures)
#    - [Permission Model](ca://s?q=Explain_Permission_Model)
#    - [Audit Logging](ca://s?q=Explain_Audit_Logging)
#    - [Threat Classification](ca://s?q=Explain_Threat_Classification)
#
#===============================================================================
#  FUNCTION OVERVIEW:
#
#    - generate_token(subject, ttl)
#         Issues authentication token.
#
#    - validate_token(token)
#         Validates token expiration.
#
#    - hash(data)
#         Computes SHA‑256 hash.
#
#    - sign(key, data)
#         Computes HMAC signature.
#
#    - register_permissions(subject, perms)
#         Assigns permissions.
#
#    - check_permission(subject, perm)
#         Validates permission access.
#
#    - audit(subject, action, meta)
#         Records audit event.
#
#    - classify_threat(event)
#         Assigns threat level.
#
#    - snapshot()
#         Returns security engine state.
#
#===============================================================================
#  THREAT EVENT FORMAT:
#
#    {
#      "unauthorized": true/false,
#      "integrity_failure": true/false,
#      "rate_limit_exceeded": true/false,
#      "sandbox_violation": true/false
#    }
#
#===============================================================================
#  RELATED MODULES:
